Provenance of the crate hclconf

Source: written in Hune from section 13 of the specification (docs/06-configuration-operation.md).
The engine is not a copy of another engine or repository.

The files and the modules are original: syntax.rs, kinds.rs, fsio.rs and secret.rs. A comparison with another strict
HCL engine found no copied code. It counted the code lines of 30 characters or more, with no comment lines. 37 of
the 1,015 code lines of src/ have the same text as a line of the other crate. Most of them are derive attributes,
use lines and function signatures. 1 of the 330 code lines of tests/ has the same text. Some names, constants and
messages are the same because the specification gives them: `CapturedEnvironment::capture_and_clear`, the value
`<not read>` and the error text for a secret in clear text (13.14).

The crate has its own parser of the HCL subset of 13.3. It does not depend on hcl-rs, url or ipnet.
The crate has no dependency. Its licence is the licence of the workspace (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Edition: 2021. The crate stays on the edition 2021 because src/env.rs calls std::env::remove_var.
This function is unsafe from the edition 2024, and each crate of the workspace forbids unsafe code
(3.4, rule R5; 17.1).

The three behaviours of 13.1 are built in. They are part of the first version of this crate:

1. A duration has exactly one integer and one unit (ms, s, m or h). The text "1m 30s", the unit
   us and the unit ns are not valid.
2. A block can depend on a mode key, as an attribute can.
3. A boolean key can be a mode key.

Only src/env.rs reads the environment (3.4, rule R2). The tests of the crate are in src/ and in tests/.
